1. PROJECT IN ONE LINE
   ==================================================

An institution submits an application and supporting documents through the AICTE portal; our AI scrutiny layer performs preliminary validation and cross-checking, produces evidence-linked findings, and presents the results to an authorized AICTE officer for manual verification and final regulatory decision-making.

CORE PRINCIPLE:

AI = Preliminary Check + Decision Support

OFFICER = Verification + Final Decision

==================================================
2. ACTUAL PROBLEM BEING SOLVED

AICTE officers may need to examine applications and many supporting documents manually.

This can involve repetitive checking such as:

- Checking whether required documents are present
- Checking document completeness
- Checking dates and expiry
- Comparing information between documents
- Comparing application information with documents
- Comparing documents with previous institutional records
- Identifying mismatched identifiers
- Detecting duplicate documents
- Identifying potential anomalies
- Checking applicable regulatory requirements
- Identifying cases requiring additional verification

The purpose of this platform is to perform these preliminary repetitive checks before the officer manually reviews the application.

The platform should help officers spend less time on routine checking and more time on cases requiring human judgement.

